# Component reuse — variant-first rule

Figma build order: design system → atoms → sections → pages.

**Before creating any component**, check `src/registry/components.json` and `src/components/`. If the shape already exists and you only need a small visual difference (color, size, layout flip, dark/light), add a **prop** to the existing file. Never create a second file for the same visual pattern.

---

## Decision tree — variant or new file?

```
Does a component with this visual shape already exist?
│
├─ YES → Is the difference only color, dark/light, size, or copy?
│        ├─ YES → Add/extend a prop (variant, isDark, size, tone…). Do NOT create a new file.
│        └─ NO  → Is the structure meaningfully different (new DOM shape, different layout)?
│                 ├─ YES → Create ONE new component. Register it in components.json.
│                 └─ NO  → It's still a variant. Add a prop.
│
└─ NO → Create ONE new component. Register it. Never paste one-off markup into a page file.
```

---

## Atoms (`src/components/ui/`) — existing variant props

| Component | Existing variants / props to use |
|---|---|
| `Button` | `variant`: primary / ghost / secondary / link · `tone`: dark / light · `size`: lg / md / sm |
| `Heading` | `variant`: h1 / h2 / h3 / h4 / eyebrow · `color`: default / white / muted / inherit |
| `Text` | `variant`: body-lg / body / small / caption / button · `color`: default / muted / white / inherit |
| `Card` | `variant`: bordered / dark / outlined / glass |
| `BlogCard` | `variant`: dark / light · `layout`: stacked / featured |

**Do not** add a second Button, a page-specific heading component, or a `DarkCard.astro` alongside `Card.astro`.
Extend the prop surface of the existing file instead.

---

## Sections (`src/components/widgets/`) — one widget per pattern

| Pattern | Widget | Key props |
|---|---|---|
| Interior page hero (homepage design system) | `PageHero` | eyebrow, titleLead, titleAccent, body, ctaText/ctaHref, secondaryCtaText/secondaryCtaHref, showCtas, image (CMS cover), default slot |
| Whole copy-driven page (hero → sections → FAQs → related → CTA) | `ContentPageView` | page: `ContentPage` from `src/data/*.ts` |
| Single customer quote band | `QuoteBand` (atom `PullQuote`) | quote, attribution, eyebrow |
| Label / value data table | `PhaseTable` | columns, rows |
| Facts list (label / value rows) | `DetailRows` | eyebrow, headingLead, headingStrong, lead, rows |
| Map + directions | `MapDirections` | mapSrc, mapTitle, caption, lead, directions, ctaText/ctaHref |
| Icon / title / description columns | `FeatureColumns` | eyebrow, headingLead, headingStrong, lead, items, columns |
| Numbered label grid (communities, areas) | `TagGrid` | eyebrow, headingLead, headingStrong, lead, items |
| Dark CTA closer | `CTABanner` | heading, note |
| FAQ accordion | `FAQs` | eyebrow, title, titleStrong, items · `<div slot="bg">` controls surface color |
| Blog listing / more articles (Sanity) | `BlogGrid` | posts, eyebrow, headingLead/Strong, lead, featured, surface |


If Figma's FAQ (or hero, CTA…) looks slightly different on one page, **restyle that widget and pass the difference as a prop**.
Do not create `HomeFAQ.astro`, `ServicesCTA.astro`, `AboutHero.astro`, etc.

---

## Content pages — data, not files

Interior pages whose copy comes from a content doc (Collision Repair services, Had an Accident topics, …) render through **one** template, `ContentPageView`:

- Copy lives in `src/data/<group>.ts` as `ContentPage` objects (shape in `src/data/contentPage.ts`). Add a page = add an object there plus a 3-line route file `<ContentPageView page={getContentPage('/route/')} />`.
- Do **not** write page-specific markup, a per-group template, or repeat FAQ / CTA wiring in route files.
- `PageHero` and the split `CTABanner` default to the sitewide buttons, closing subtitle and silver band (`src/config/cta.ts`, `CONTACT`). Pass those props only to override (e.g. the homepage CTA).
- Need a section the template lacks? Add one new section `type` + widget, register it, then reuse it everywhere.

---

## Surface / background — use `slot="bg"` or `isDark`, not a new component

When the same section needs a different background on different pages, pass the surface inline:

```astro
<!-- ✅ correct — one FAQs widget, surface swapped via slot -->
<FAQs title="…" items={faqs}>
  <div slot="bg" class="absolute inset-0 bg-card"></div>
</FAQs>

<!-- ✅ correct — dark vs light toggle via prop -->
<CTABanner isDark={false} heading="…" />

<!-- ❌ wrong — new file just to change background color -->
<ServiceFAQs title="…" items={faqs} />
<LightCTABanner heading="…" />
```

---

## Registering new components

Any genuinely new visual shape (different DOM structure, not just different styles) → create **one** file, then add an entry to `src/registry/components.json`:

```json
{
  "id": "P-XX",
  "name": "Human-readable name",
  "figmaNames": ["Figma frame or component name"],
  "shape": "One-sentence description of the DOM shape",
  "component": "ComponentName",
  "import": "~/components/widgets/ComponentName.astro",
  "props": { "propName": "type — description" },
  "notes": "When to use vs the nearest existing pattern"
}
```

---

## Layout and card rules

- Do **not** pick a layout (band vs grid vs cards) based on item count. Figma decides the layout.
- Cards with a link or button: `flex flex-col h-full` on the card · `flex-1` on the body · `mt-auto` on the CTA → links line up regardless of copy length.
